---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
---
<Base title={"Therapy Insurance & FAQs in Utah | Tangible Therapy"} description={"Learn about Blue Cross, DMBA, PEHP, Regence, Cigna, and Aetna with our Utah County therapists. Tangible Mental Health answers your insurance and pricing FAQs."}>
<section class="sec t-white h-medium has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:20;--mrows:10">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:1/5/21/23;--m:1/2/11/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><figure class="img fill"><img src="/images/insurance-12-x-7-999-in-2a5247.jpg" alt="Chart titled &quot;Insurances We Accept,&quot; showing accepted insurance plans for seven individuals. Green check marks indicate acceptance; red Xs indicate rejection." width="6250" height="4166" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
</div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#acb9ac" /></section>

<section class="sec t-black h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/4/26;--m:1/2/4/10"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">✺ Frequently asked questions ✺</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/2/14/13;--m:5/2/13/10"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>Am I covered by insurance?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Currently our practice works with, United Healthcare, Blue Cross Blue Shield, Regence, EMI, DMBA, PEHP, &amp; Select Health. This is a covered service under all major insurances, however we recommend that you reach out to your insurance company to understand specific copay/deductible amounts.</p></div></details><details><summary>What is the cost without insurance?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Our cash pay rate is $150 per session. </p></div></details><details><summary>How is Tangible different from other therapy practices?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Tangible is built on the core philosophy of offering skills-based therapy. Our therapists are dedicated to equipping you with practical skills that not only facilitate your healing process but also enable you to sustain your wellbeing long after therapy has ended.</p></div></details></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/15/14/26;--m:13/2/21/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>How do I know if my therapist is a good fit?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Ensuring that you are compatible with your therapist is a critical part of the therapeutic process. We are happy to offer a 15-minute free consultation call with any therapist to determine if they are the right one for you.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you work with ecclesiastical leaders (Bishops)?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Yes, we are more than happy to coordinate care. Please let us know when scheduling an appointment and we will take care of the rest.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long will it take?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Duration of care can depend on a wide variety of factors. However, most people see significant progress in 8-12 weeks. </p></div></details></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</Base>
